-- title:
--   The common frame (`fx_frame`)
-- statement:
--   The common frame: the set-up, a `FineBody6`-style call, the tear-down.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegAxA2`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.Ax.fx_frame (w f a y : ℕ) (hF0 : dF ≠ 0) (hFA : dF ≠ dA) (hA0 : dA ≠ 0)
--       (hSet : SetupS Isym tbl stUp stDn ![dF] dA desc ![descFine w f a y] Cs)
--       {e : Fin Pp} {g : List GI → List GI} {Ce : ℝ}
--       (he : ∀ (s : IState HS) (F : Fin HS → List ℤ) (zs : List GI) (l : List ℤ),
--         (∀ j, j ≠ 0 → j ≠ dF → F j = []) → F dF = descFine w f a y → F 0 = gflat zs ++ l →
--         zs.length = a * (2 ^ f * y) → GB w zs →
--         ∃ c : ℕ, IRuns Isym tbl (.call e) (encK s F)
--           (encK s (Function.update F 0 (gflat (g zs) ++ l))) c ∧ (c : ℝ) ≤ Ce) :
--       PassOK Isym tbl (fxSt stUp stDn e) dA desc
--         (fun L => L.length = a * (2 ^ f * y) ∧ GB w L) g (2 * Cs + Ce)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** `A`-line axis program (`AxisUA6`), part 2: a fine exposure as a `PassOK` step
--
--   `fxSt stUp stDn e = stUp; call e; stDn`: the set-up pushes the fine descriptor
--   `descFine w f a y` onto the fine stack `dF` (computed from the axis descriptor on `dA`,
--   `SetupS` with the one register `dF`), the exposure `e` (`FineBody6`, forward `eF` or back `eB`),
--   the tear-down pops it.
--
--   **`fxF_ok`** / **`fxB_ok`**: the step computes `blkT (2^f) y a` / `blkT y (2^f) a` on stack `0`
--   at cost `2 Cs + C₀ cFine w f a y`.
